slides.explanationMarkdown:
Store serializes replacements through Queue, then Read rev reads the stored revision inside that operation.
Queue supplies the request's expected revision to Match?; Read rev supplies the current revision.
No rejects a stale replacement without creating Temp JSON, calling Rename, or incrementing the revision.
Only after a match does Temp JSON hold the complete replacement for atomic commit.
Another replacement cannot enter between Read rev, Match?, and Rename; they remain one serialized Store operation.

```typescript
if (expectedRevision !== currentRevision) {
  throw new Error("Revision conflict");
}
```
